    "answer": {
      "short": "630 passengers",
      "worked": "Let $x$ be the initial number of passengers. After the first station, there are $\\frac{x}{2}+135$ passengers. The second departure is $\\frac{x}{3}$, referring to the passengers who arrived at the first station.\n$$\\begin{align*}\\left(\\frac{x}{2}+135\\right)-\\frac{x}{3}+110&=350\\\\\\frac{x}{6}+245&=350\\\\\\frac{x}{6}&=105\\\\x&=630\\end{align*}$$\nThe train left Alston with 630 passengers.",
      "solutionDiagrams": []
